{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "5f6dfa08-e755-8366-9e65-796d742ebcb8",
  "created_at": "2026-02-11T10:41:30-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Rafael Morales",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:38:33-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:38:36-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, Kevin. My name is Rafael Morales. I'm calling about a drainage problem at my mother's house, 305 Kingston Avenue, up on the Hill. Sorry, I'm in a stairwell, the signal's bad in the apartment, so it echoes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:38:50-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, I can hear you okay. Three-oh-five Kingston. What's going on there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:38:55-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a pipe at the curb, in front of her house, and water runs out of it. Not from rain. It's been dry since, uh, the fourth, Wednesday the fourth, I'm sure of it. And it's running anyway, every day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:39:10-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so water coming out of a pipe at the curb, no storm. Got it, I'm writing that down."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:39:17-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. And with the cold, it freezes. It runs across the sidewalk and turns into a sheet of ice. [line breaks up] my mother is eighty-one, she can't walk out there. Yesterday morning I [inaudible] salt, and by four o'clock it was glazed again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:39:33-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You broke up there for a second. You put salt down yesterday morning and it iced back over by four?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:39:41-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Salted at, I think eight-thirty, eight forty-five. Iced again by four. And now the water is moving down toward the neighbor's garage. Not to her garage, the neighbor's, the one to the left as you face the house. It's pooling at the door."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:39:57-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, toward the neighbor's garage. Is it getting inside, or just pooling out front?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:40:03-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just pooling so far. But it's going to freeze there too. Look, this isn't the first time I've called about it. I want to know when somebody last came by. Because my mother says nobody has been out, and I'd like a date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:40:19-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. Let me pull up the address. [pause] Kingston Avenue, three-oh-five. Hmm, I'm not seeing a crew visit logged in the system for that one, at least not recently. I don't want to read you something wrong, so I'll have the supervisor check the paper records too."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:40:36-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So nothing logged. That's what I thought. Nobody came, and it's just been running."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:40:42-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "On my screen, nothing recent, yeah. I'll put in a request now, mark it as ice on the sidewalk and water heading to a neighbor's property, so it gets looked at sooner. Could be a leak in a line, could be something else, a crew will have to look."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:41:00-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Please note it's an elderly resident, and the ice is right where she'd walk to the car."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:41:07-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Noted. Elderly resident, ice on the sidewalk. Best number to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:41:12-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-six-four. That's mine, Rafael. Not hers."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:41:16-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-six-four, Rafael. Got it. Somebody will call you back about when they're heading out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:41:22-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. I'd appreciate it today if possible. Thank you, Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T10:41:26-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got it. Stay safe on those stairs."
    }
  ],
